solar-system-model-answer-text-2 = T²/a³ for all eight planets — from { $value } to { $value2 }: nearly the same, as Kepler’s third law says, though the planets’ distances differ 78 times.
solar-system-model-answer-text-3 = Voyager 1 on 14 February 1990 was { $value } m off in the model. From there the Earth is the same 1.8 mm grain; on the picture it took, it fills 0.12 of a pixel. Carl Sagan, whose idea the picture was, said of the dot: “That’s here. That’s home. That’s us.”
